<problem boxed>
  <p>The formula <m>C = \frac{5}{9}(F-32),</m> where <m>F \ge -459.67</m> expresses the Celsius temperature <m>C</m> as a function of Fahrenheit temperature <m>F.</m></p>

  <part>
    <p>Find the formula for the inverse function.
      <br />
      <answer name="ans1">
        <label><m>C^{-1}(F) =</m></label>
        <math name="sol1">(9/5) F + 32</math>
      </answer>
    </p>
  </part>

  <part>
    <p>What is the domain of the inverse function <m>C^{-1}</m> ?
      <br />
      <answer name="ans2" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.1" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
        <label>Answer (in interval notation):</label>
        <math name="sol2">[-273.15, infinity)</math>
      </answer>
    </p>
  </part>

  <givenAnswer>
    <ol>
      <li><p><m>C^{-1}(F) = $sol1</m></p></li>
      <li><p><m>$sol2</m></p></li>
    </ol>
  </givenAnswer>
</problem>



